# Display profiles, applied by kanshi on start and whenever a monitor is
# plugged in or removed. A profile lists a set of monitors and is applied when
# exactly that set is connected, which is what makes docking and undocking a
# laptop work without touching the sway config.
#
# Match monitors on their EDID "Make Model Serial" string (see
# `swaymsg -t get_outputs`) so each panel keeps its place whichever port it is
# on, or on the connector name (DP-1, HDMI-A-1, eDP-1, ...). `nwg-displays`
# (Super+d) can write these for you. With no profiles kanshi simply idles.
#
# profile docked {
#	output "Vendor Model Serial" mode 1920x1080@60Hz position 0,0 scale 1 enable
#	output "Vendor Model Serial" mode 1920x1080@60Hz position 1920,0 scale 1 enable
# }
#
# profile undocked {
#	output eDP-1 enable
# }
